WEBVTT

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:06.520
We're done for...
This is the end...

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.270
Amnesia Effect!

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.210
Play The Game...

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:31.800
It's no use.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.630
The wind's too strong.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.490
Let me go!

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:46.180
[Wind Report]
 Hakone City, Ashigarashimo District, Kanagawa Prefecture 
Strong winds in this area that began after 5:00 PM have peaked and are projected to subside within ten minutes.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.500
The strong winds around Hakone are

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.190
thought to subside within 
approximately ten minutes.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.620
The wind will die down 
within ten minutes.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.770
Let's stay calm and wait.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.700
Don't!

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.740
You'll get flung off!

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.450
Hang in there! 
It'll be okay!

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.710
Just a little longer...

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.590
In two minutes, rescuers will arrive.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.010
We <i>will</i> save everyone!

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.070
I'm scared and afraid. 
Please come save us soon!

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:23.040
I'm scared and afraid. 
Please come save us soon!
Help will be here in two minutes.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:22.350
Help will be here in two minutes.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:23.970
Help will be here in two minutes. 
Please stay calm and follow 
the rescuers' instructions.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.370
We'll all be saved!

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.390
We're done for!

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.510
There's no way we'll be saved!

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.510
I don't believe you!

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.610
Calm down!

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:35.300
I didn't believe in 
GALAXTERs before, either,

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:39.660
but this saved my life when 
I got into an accident.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.230
Have faith and wait.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.730
GALAX won't abandon us!

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.580
Help will arrive 
in 20 seconds. 
Hang in there!

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.300
Help will be here 
in twenty seconds.

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:55.260
I have faith.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.490
Here they are!

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.470
Help has arrived.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:04.770
It's just like GALAX said.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:06.310
Yay!

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.310
Thank goodness!

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.930
We'll now begin rescue operations!

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.750
Please let the children 
and the elderly evacuate first!

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:28.410
I'm sorry to ask, 
but can children evacuate first?

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.330
Sure, that's fine.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.290
Of course.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.850
It's okay.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.010
Don't be scared.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:35.490
Okay.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.300
You're not human, are you?

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.590
Okay, this planet is finished.

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:15.000
No one... No one will be spared.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.680
Amnesia Effect!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.850
Go, Bird!

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:24.030
Everyone will go up in a big, red blaze!

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.670
Burning Rain!

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.130
Everyone believed they'd be saved.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.460
There were lots 
of people who use GALAX,

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.550
and they explained 
what was going on to us.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.300
GALAX's information was accurate.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.240
It seems some of the rescuers 
were GALAXTERs, too.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.130
It was everywhere.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:54.020
Good work, everyone.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.730
The world has been updated.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:03.390
There were no victims.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:07.080
Rui, it was thanks to 
your timely decision-making.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.330
Is something the matter, Rui?

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.870
I wasn't the one who saved them.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.420
It was CROWDS.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:19.590
It's all your guys' fault. 
Do you even get that?

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:20.920
What do you mean?

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.840
You guys are primitive.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.840
Burning....

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.260
Go, B-B-B-B-B-Bird!

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:28.970
What?!

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:46.280
Oh, my! MESSY's way too sensitive!

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.910
Yeah, isn't it awesome?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.620
MESSY seems to like 
changing its shape.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:55.040
Oh, MESSY's acting weird today.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:58.120
C'mon, Utsutsu. Try it, too.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.860
I'm gloomy...

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:04.160
Man, we've got way 
too much free time.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.920
We've been beating 
MESS-chan up all this time,

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.130
but we're way too friendly 
with this MESS-chan!

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:11.260
Oh, Jou-chan.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:14.040
You're looking way too scary!

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.390
A strange alien?

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.440
Yeah.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.940
My powers didn't have any effect.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.080
It's a violent one, too.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:26.110
It camouflaged itself as a random 
passerby and stabbed a lot of people.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:27.590
Could it also be...

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:31.780
Multiple Assaults in Tachikawa Area 
Suspects All Deny Involvement 
Suspects Claim  Bodies Suddenly Appeared in Front of Them

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.250
...responsible for all of them?

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.530
I wouldn't be surprised.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.830
It said,

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.660
"No one will be spared."

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.540
"Everyone will go up 
in a big, red blaze."

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.290
and "You're all to blame."

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:44.070
So yeah.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.260
What does this all mean?

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:49.590
It was pretty tough.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.260
You fought against it, Jou-san?

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.760
Yeah. I didn't manage 
to finish it off today,

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.710
but I will, for sure, next time.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.890
Still, something bothers me.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.060
Remember what JJ 
said a while back?

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.480
He said, "A bird with sundered 
wings has wandered in."

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:07.400
Yes.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.170
I've been wondering 
what he meant.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.200
It had a NOTE.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.450
A NOTE like this?

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.580
Yeah...

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:19.160
You mean, it might be 
a Gatchaman like us?

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:20.390
I wonder.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.880
Are there more 
Gatchaman than just us?

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.300
OD, Paiman, you know 
something, don't you?

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.800
It was really tall.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.470
Long, tangled hair and 
a diamond-shaped tail.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:33.810
Who is it?

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.560
Pai-Pai? D-san?

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.930
You're acting weird.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:46.690
The crazed bird 
has appeared once more,

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:50.740
scattering the innocent with iron.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.780
Hands off this one, guys!

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.660
How can you say that?

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.910
There's already been several deaths!

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.950
We don't know for certain 
that an alien is behind them!

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.370
But if it is,

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.500
we have to deal with it, 
as Gatchaman.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:06.130
Listen, do not become involved!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.620
That's a direct order!

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:10.920
I'm talking especially to you, 
Newbie! Don't do anything!

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:13.260
Boo!

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.510
Sugane, Utsutsu, keep an eye on her!

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.480
That will be all! 
No more discussion!

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:23.210
Are you scared?

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.310
You're pathetic, Leader.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.610
I can't let this pass.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.440
Let's split up and find it.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.320
Stop, all of you.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.240
What?

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.070
You, too, Hajime-chan.  
Do as Pai-Pai says.

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:42.160
Newbie.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.410
I'm Hajime!

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.460
What's on your mind?

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.670
What else? 
What we should do next?

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.010
We have to do something!

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:55.350
I mean, the bad Gatchaman 
said it's all our fault, right?

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.930
Isn't that really bad?!

00:08:58.930 --> 00:08:59.690
Jou-san?

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.140
If we don't do something...

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.100
Miss, don't worry.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:06.110
I'll settle the score 
with that insane bird.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.390
That's not it!

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:09.610
I'm not talking about that!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.490
I'm gloomy...

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:23.120
It can't be helped, Pai-Pai.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:24.910
That's all you 
could've said to them.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:29.080
I'm the only one 
who understands.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.880
We're done for!

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.300
Once it comes, this planet 
will be wiped out!

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:39.720
Calm down, Pai-Pai!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.430
How can I calm down?!

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:43.970
I'm talking about <i>it</i>!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:47.600
It's a demon who's destroyed 
countless planets..

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:50.480
And it doesn't just destroy them.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.110
It never gets its own hands dirty.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:58.280
It loves watching the planets' 
inhabitants destroy each other.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.530
If only I'd managed to defeat it...

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:02.910
OD, don't be rash.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.450
You know what I mean, right?

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.790
If you spread <i>your</i> wings...

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:07.810
I know.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.290
If that happens, 
all will be destroyed.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:11.840
I know...

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:15.700
I also lost my best 
friend because of it...

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.510
I don't want to experience 
that ever again!

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.600
But why did it come

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.930
to this backwaters planet 
under protective observation?

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.140
It probably found out...

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.270
Found out what?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.510
A trigger that'll cause humans 
to destroy each other.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.800
"Go up in a big, red blaze"...

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.100
That must be the hint.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:40.110
It'll be sure to guide this planet 
to destruction, slowly but surely.

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:44.640
That's the ultimate pleasure 
for Berg-Katze, after all...

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.080
Sugane, I'm going to do it.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.820
Next time, I <i>will</i> beat it up.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.430
Of course. I will come with you.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:09.560
I only became a Gatchaman 
because of you, Jou-san.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.530
{smirk} I've heard that line 
too many times.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:15.570
Hey, Sugane, come for a drink?

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:18.030
Like I keep saying, I'm a minor.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:19.700
Oh, right.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.680
Well, off I go, then.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:26.120
Who knows how long 
you can have fun drinking?

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:32.540
Why are the assaults our fault?

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.630
I'm kind of hung up over it.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.590
Pai-Pai and D-san were 
acting weird, too.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:42.320
That was the first time I saw 
D-san acting so serious, too.

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:45.010
Oh, wow! This area's crazy.

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.720
The police are there,

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.100
and the self-defense forces 
are across from them.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.060
There's the riot police, the fire station,

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.480
and the city hall is that way, too.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.680
Isn't Tachikawa going to be okay, 
no matter what?

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.780
Don't you think, Utsutsu-chan?

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.090
Utsutsu-chan, are you 
always this quiet?

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:05.740
It's like you're here, 
but not really.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.900
That's how...

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.700
Huh, what? What's how?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.250
Oh, sorry.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.790
That's how my body is.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.980
Huh? What do you mean?

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:18.550
This body is a copy.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.570
You're a copy, Utsutsu-chan?

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.800
I can make any number of copies.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.050
Wow!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.130
I wish I could, too.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:28.100
You can't.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:30.770
I can because my body is weird.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.770
Wow, that's great.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:34.940
It's not great.

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.190
I see.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:37.610
You don't like it.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:38.730
I don't.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.530
I can't touch anyone.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:42.950
Because I hurt them.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.910
That's the kind of life form I am.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:50.700
So even if I'm happy, I soon 
want to cry, disappear, or...

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.350
Or hurt someone?

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.210
Aren't I scary?

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.500
Hey, Utsutsu-chan.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.050
What does that streetlight 
look like to you?

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.260
A streetlight is a streetlight.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:10.040
From here, it looks 
round and smiley.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.950
Utsutsu-chan, you're just 
fine the way you are.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:16.650
That's what I think.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:20.210
I mean, you're so cute!

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:22.860
I'm happy, no matter what.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:24.820
I don't want to vanish.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.660
It's all okay!

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:28.870
Liar...

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:35.250
I want to talk to the real 
Utsutsu-chan, someday!

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:41.260
What's wrong, Utsutsu?

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.380
Head... hurts.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.970
Is Hajime-chan saying 
something to you?

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:49.350
I don't want copies anymore...

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.910
Yeah.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:53.140
But we're all like that.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.060
Having special powers is something

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.500
to be glad about, but sad as well.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.440
Ninomiya Rui-kun.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:07.800
You have gained the power 
to materialize a person's soul.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:14.700
Th-This is my soul?

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:18.500
Yes, as long as you have this,

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.630
all of your wishes can come true.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.250
My wishes....

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.260
Good morning, Rui-Rui.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:32.550
That's a lot of sweat!

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.490
Did you have a nightmare?

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:36.850
So scary!

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.270
No, not really.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.770
I saw.

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:45.990
You seem to be using 
what I gave you.

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:47.070
Yeah.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:52.740
Everyone seems to say 
it's really great.

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:54.910
Do you think you 
can update the world?

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:58.160
I'm grateful to you, Alien-kun.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.310
You're welcome, Primitive-chan.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:01.670
But, you know...

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:06.010
If everyone finds out 
that their hope, GALAX,

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:11.680
is in a contract with someone 
like me, what would they think?

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:13.950
Confirm biometrics.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.080
Good morning, X.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.210
Good evening, Rui.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:29.780
It appears all suspects are continuing 
to deny their involvement.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:32.280
No one remembers 
committing murder.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:35.200
They feel it's as though 
someone took over their body.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.870
What is it, Rui-Rui? Huh?

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:39.910
Nothing...

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.380
Online forums indicate 
increased interest

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.260
in preventing these incidents 
before they happen using GALAX.

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:48.710
But GALAX isn't up to the task!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:51.090
Hey, Rui-Rui, do you want 
to know the true culprit?

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:54.570
It's the human heart!

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:55.640
Heart?

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:56.970
Yes.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:01.560
The black hearts you 
foolish humans all possess.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.910
They're all overflowing 
and making people kill each other.

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:07.710
That's why these incidents 
will never cease!

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.070
It's a crisis!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:11.060
It's scary!

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:13.320
It's fun, isn't it, Rui-Rui?

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:15.760
Let's start a revolution together.

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:20.910
Okay, I'm off for some 
exercise outside.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.250
Bye-bye.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:28.460
We still have no information 
about that alien.

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:32.130
As for Gatchaman, I am scanning 
security camera footage—

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.890
That's no longer necessary. 
They don't exist, after all.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.350
We won't ask for help 
from any heroes.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.930
I will handle it, myself.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:43.940
Your goal has been to have 
a bloodless revolution.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:45.650
I know!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:48.440
But I can't let it 
run loose any longer.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:53.120
X, you know why I formed 
the Hundred, don't you?

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:56.660
I have to make 
the world update itself.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.200
My Hundred and you:

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.270
We're the ones 
who can change the world.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:05.370
I am going to make 
the world accelerate.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:10.340
Oh, hey. You're working!

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.960
Oh, Hyuuga, Kaede!

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:17.640
Hey, wasn't that miracle rescue 
on the ropeway yesterday amazing?

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:20.060
Here we go again about GALAX.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.970
That was amazing, yeah.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:23.680
Right?

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.560
If it's that great,

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:29.480
shouldn't we let GALAX handle 
police work and politics?

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.900
That's not true.

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:33.770
But isn't it amazing 
that it can resolve things

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:35.160
before anyone shows up?

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.320
It's amazing, but it's not good.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.240
Oh, yeah? Why?

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.330
Because that'd be kind of sad 
if that's all there is.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:44.710
Yeah... That's it.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.420
Hajime-chan!

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:48.580
Oh, Baracchi!

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.420
"Baracchi"?

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:54.510
It's Kuwabara-san, chief of the 
Tachikawa Fire Department.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.590
Hey, Baracchi. You would save 
people, no matter what, right?

00:17:58.590 --> 00:17:59.390
What?

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.680
Even if the world 
goes up in a big, red blaze,

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.140
you'd save people, right?

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:06.100
Y-Yeah. Of course!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.350
See?

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:14.570
I give up!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.360
Just cry there!

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:19.220
Mommy!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.880
Mommy!

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.310
That's...

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:40.840
Hey, stop!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:45.180
Accident at crossing 
before Toyosu Station!

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:46.730
Beginning rescue 
operations immediately!

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:48.600
Understood.

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:53.020
A traffic accident has occurred 
in front of Toyosu Station. 
Many people have been injured. 
Will you help?

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:58.820
<b>A traffic accident has occurred in front of Toyosu Station. 
Many people have been injured. Will you help?</b>

00:18:56.900 --> 00:19:02.020
Eight GALAXTERs in the area 
have agreed to assist.

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:04.740
How horrible!

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:06.200
Can you hear me?

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.610
Please hang in there!

00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:13.590
Why did it... do such a thing?

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.020
Look out!

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.170
There she is!

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:21.880
Okay!

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:23.410
It wasn't me!

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:25.110
I don't know anything!

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:29.080
Amnesia Effect!

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.900
Rui-Rui, you're teary-eyed!

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.760
Too bad! So sad!

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:38.540
I guess you couldn't 
be a hero today!

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:42.300
It's finally begun, Rui-Rui!

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:45.380
A festival, festival, festival!

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:46.860
Yay!

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:53.310
Rui, unfortunately, there were 
seventeen casualties.

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:55.580
It's my fault.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:56.840
All my fault!

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.710
Why did I get its power?!

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:01.230
What have I been doing?!

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:06.910
What have I been doing 
all this time?!

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.590
Jou, you're in an 
unusually good mood.

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.390
Did something good happen?

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:13.320
Nope, nothing really.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:16.010
It's like you're back 
to your old self.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:20.530
Alan, I haven't changed at all.

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:23.830
<i>As for the suspect in custody, 
a housewife, she claims</i>

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:26.370
<i>she doesn't remember anything, 
including getting into the vehicle.</i>

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.000
<i>She is denying any involvement.</i>

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:32.070
<i>However, witnesses say 
she was upset and scolding</i>

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:33.320
<i>her child right before the incident.</i>

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:39.250
<i>Police believe this incident 
to be a mass assault</i>

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:34.680
It's <i>it</i>.

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:35.210
Huh?

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:39.400
It's like everyone is stressed out.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.920
<i>and are continuing 
their investigation.</i>

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:43.090
Oh, look: "Expectations Higher 
Than Ever for GALAX."

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:46.370
It's like our disaster prevention 
department might as well not exist.

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:49.920
Like, we're all fine 
as long as GALAX exists?

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:51.150
It can't be helped.

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:52.590
The enemy is too strong.

00:20:52.590 --> 00:20:54.100
Huh? Enemy?

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.940
What do you mean, Jou-san?

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.310
Oh, sorry.

00:20:57.740 --> 00:21:01.780
Well, what's the point in us civil 
servants worrying about it?

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:03.860
Man, what scary times we live in.

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.590
I guess we can only 
count on GALAX.

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:08.810
Heroes can't be found 
anywhere anymore, anyway.

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:10.620
Oh, you going home already, Jou?

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:12.830
Huh? You're kidding, right, Jou-san?

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.920
The match isn't finished yet.

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:16.280
Are you running away?

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:17.880
Me? Running away?

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:20.040
Don't be ridiculous.

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:22.380
I just have something 
I've got to do.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.260
Hey, Jou-san!

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:31.810
There's a hero right here.

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:34.480
Don't underestimate Gatchaman.
